**Date:** 11 November 2026 · **Deciders:** support desk · **Replaces:** [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)

## Context

Decision 0001 merged reports on the subject line alone. Ticket #4471 shows what that costs: 412 reports were
merged into one ticket, and they describe three different problems. The same subjects ("Wrong day on the
invite", "Month and day swapped?") appear in all of them. Intake's browser guess was wrong too. The split is on
[the #4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471-three-problems).

## Decision

Two reports are the same issue when they have the same cause. The cause comes from the tenant: where it writes
dates, and which booking form it runs (`causeOf` in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`). Subject lines and intake tags do not
decide a merge.

Reports the desk reads differently from their tenant's cause (the one-day shifts) are counted where they are
filed and listed under their own problem.

## Consequences

- Triage needs the tenant, not only the subject. It is slower than a subject match, but each ticket is one problem.
- Engineering gets one ticket per cause, each with its own count.
- A fix for one cause no longer closes reports that belong to another.

